Description: Don't abort when the compositor re-sends linux-dmabuf feedback
 zwp_linux_dmabuf_feedback_v1 may be sent again at any time (the protocol
 allows it). WorldLink/Hyprland re-sends it when outputs come and go, e.g. when
 the screen is turned off by the idle daemon and back on. The main_device event
 then hits assert(ctx->gbm == NULL) and the portal aborts — every 10 minutes on
 a multi-GPU PC with "turn off the screen after 10 minutes".
 The compositor's render device does not change while it runs, so keep the
 GBM device that is already open and ignore the repeated main_device.
Author: SekaiOS <https://github.com/caterpillar321/sekaios>
Forwarded: no
--- a/src/screencast/wlr_screencast.c
+++ b/src/screencast/wlr_screencast.c
@@ -642,7 +642,12 @@ static void linux_dmabuf_feedback_handle_main_device(void *data,
 
 	logprint(DEBUG, "wlroots: linux_dmabuf_feedback_handle_main_device called");
 
-	assert(ctx->gbm == NULL);
+	if (ctx->gbm != NULL) {
+		// Feedback re-sent (outputs changed) — the render device is the same
+		// for the compositor's lifetime, keep the one already in use.
+		logprint(DEBUG, "wlroots: main device sent again, keeping the current render node");
+		return;
+	}
 
 	dev_t device;
 	assert(device_arr->size == sizeof(device));
